      "finalAnswer": "Confirmed against the actual files. Here's everything added or changed this session:\n\n## Source files\n\n**`src/core/format.ts`**\n- `formatDuration(ms): string` — new function, formats a millisecond duration compactly (`950ms` / `12s` / `3m 05s` / `1h 02m`) for display in the tooltip and sidebar card.\n- `pad(value): string` — new private helper, zero-pads seconds/minutes so `\"3m 5s\"` reads as `\"3m 05s\"`.\n\n**`src/transcript/sessionAccumulator.ts`**\n- `SessionStats.firstActivity?: number` — new field, the earliest timestamp seen in a transcript, needed to compute session length.\n- `SessionAccumulator` private field `firstActivity` — internal running minimum backing the snapshot field.\n- `touch()` — extended to also update `firstActivity` (previously only tracked `lastActivity`).\n- `snapshot()` — extended to include `firstActivity` in the returned `SessionStats`.\n\n**`src/core/sessionView.ts`**\n- `SessionView.durationMs: number` — new field, `lastActivity - firstActivity` clamped to ≥0, `0` when either end is unknown; exposes session length to the UI.\n- `SessionView.cacheHitRate: number` — new field, share of session input tokens served from the prompt cache; `0` when there were no input tokens.\n- `cacheHitRate(totals)` — new private helper computing that ratio safely (avoids divide-by-zero).\n- `toSessionView()` — extended to populate both new fields (imports `contextTokensOf` from `transcript/types` for the ratio's denominator).\n\n**`src/ui/statusBar.ts`**\n- `buildTooltip()` — extended to append a line showing session duration and cache hit rate (`\"N prompts over 3m 05s · 75% cache hit rate · active …\"`), shown only when `durationMs > 0`.\n\n**`src/webview/main.ts`**\n- `renderActive()` — extended the sidebar card's meta line to include session duration the same way, reusing `formatDuration`.\n\n**`README.md`**\n- Status bar and sidebar bullets in the Features section updated to mention session length and cache hit rate, matching what's now actually rendered.\n\n## Test files\n\n- **`test/format.test.ts`** — `formatDuration` cases, including negative-input clamping to `\"0ms\"`.\n- **`test/sessionAccumulator.test.ts`** — `firstActivity` correctness: earliest-of-many, undefined with no timestamps, single-event equals `lastActivity`, epoch-`0` timestamp treated as real, and tool-result-only entries still advance it.\n- **`test/sessionView.test.ts`** — `durationMs` (normal case, unknown cases, equal-timestamps, negative-diff clamp) and `cacheHitRate` (0.75 case, all-empty, zero-cache-reads, fully-cached).\n- **`test/sessionStore.test.ts`** — documents that `firstActivity` on a `SessionRecord` comes only from the main transcript, while `lastActivity` also merges subagent activity (intentional asymmetry, now locked in by a test).\n\nAll 115 tests pass; both typecheck projects (`.` and `src/webview`) are clean.",
