      "finalAnswer": "Confirmed. Here's everything added or changed this session, no unmodified/pre-existing code included:\n\n**`src/webview/main.ts`**\n- `renderDuration(session)` — new function; formats session length for the sidebar card, reusing `formatDuration` instead of duplicating status-bar logic.\n- Meta line template (`<p class=\"meta\">…`) — wired `renderDuration(session)` into it so the card shows session length.\n- Import of `formatDuration` from `../core/format` — needed by the above.\n\n**`src/core/sessionView.ts`**\n- `SessionView.cacheHitRate: number` field — new field so UI code can display prompt cache effectiveness without recomputing it per-consumer.\n- `cacheHitRate(totals)` — new private helper; computes `cacheRead / (input+cacheWrite+cacheRead)`, returns `0` when there's no input data, avoiding a `NaN`.\n- `toSessionView` return object — added `cacheHitRate: cacheHitRate(record.totals)` to populate the field.\n- Import of `contextTokensOf` from `../transcript/types` — reused the existing \"total input tokens\" helper instead of re-deriving it.\n\n**`src/ui/statusBar.ts`**\n- `buildTooltip` — added a `cacheHitRate` segment to the prompt-count line, showing the rate as a percentage next to session length.\n- Gate condition — changed from `view.cacheHitRate > 0` to `contextTokensOf(view.totals) > 0`, so a session with real tokens but a genuine 0% hit rate still displays it instead of being mistaken for \"no data.\"\n- Import of `contextTokensOf` — needed for the corrected gate.\n\n**`test/sessionView.test.ts`**\n- `computes cacheHitRate as cacheRead over all input tokens` — verifies the core ratio math.\n- `defaults cacheHitRate to 0 when there are no input tokens` — verifies the zero-denominator fallback (no `NaN`).\n- `computes cacheHitRate as 1 when every input token was a cache read` — boundary case, all-cache session.\n- `computes cacheHitRate as 0 when there are input tokens but none were cache reads` — the case that exposed the status-bar gating bug; documents it's a valid, real `0`, not just the \"no data\" fallback.\n\n**`README.md`**\n- Status bar Features bullet — now mentions the hover tooltip shows session length and cache hit rate.\n- Sidebar panel Features bullet — now mentions session length is shown on the card (cache hit rate intentionally omitted here, since it's status-bar-only).",
